# Fixed 2026-09-29, defect 130's class, lane X4, on lane Y's finding.
# Symptom: a head alone at a line's end over a line at its own margin that
# fails, `if` over `print(1 +)`, `for` over `x in )`, `y = match` over
# `print(1 +)`, never told its missing body in the control arm, `check
# --permissive`, which reads the join as the program and so passed a
# bodiless `if` on. Cause: the head crossed a line, and a crossed line
# silences an absent body, since inside brackets a head's own recovery can
# run past its line; the lexer's join outside them is no recovery. The
# silence now asks for the break to be inside brackets
# (`parse/head_lines.joined_outside_brackets`), and the missing body is held
# as over any join: said in the control arm, where the lexer's refusal of the
# join is dropped, and in this arm the refusal and the line's own mistake are
# the report, as here.

function main()
    if  #~ continuation_outside_brackets
    print(1 +)  #~ expected_expression

function loop()
    for  #~ continuation_outside_brackets
    x in )  #~ expected_expression

function bound()
    y = match  #~ continuation_outside_brackets
    print(1 +)  #~ expected_expression
